{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-boltzmann-constant","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:boltzmann-constant","kind":"proposition","title":"Boltzmann constant is unity in QOU natural units","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-temperature"],"tags":["boltzmann-constant","statistical-mechanics","planck-constant"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Information.thermalEnergy","text":"boltzmann-constant.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/boltzmann-constant.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:boltzmann-constant\"></a><p>In natural QOU units, we set the Boltzmann constant to unity: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k_B = 1</code>. The quantum Planck constant <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hbar_q</code> formally replaces the classical thermal energy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">k_B T_{\\mathrm{phys}}</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  k_B \\, T_{\\mathrm{phys}} = \\hbar_q = \\frac{q-1}{q}.</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/boltzmann-constant.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"21.9.10"}
